doc15-s01-c01,doc15-s01,doc15,1,"We introduce LLaMA, a collection of foundation language models ranging from 7B to 65B parameters. We train our models on trillions of tokens, and show that it is possible to train state-of-the-art models using publicly available datasets exclusively, without resorting to proprietary and inaccessible datasets. In particular, LLaMA-13B outperforms GPT-3 (175B) on most benchmarks, and LLaMA- 65B is competitive with the best models, Chinchilla-70B and PaLM-540B. We release all our models to the research community1.",,"[-0.046905, 0.040289, 0.016507, -0.026947, -0.013126, 0.072409, -0.008561, 0.036012, -0.007499, 0.024611, 0.031424, 0.008275, 0.012064, -0.042326, -0.078815, -0.034496, -0.007892, 0.061927, -0.043173, 0.008921, 0.052903, 0.014896, -0.066842, -0.047509, 0.02822, 0.036937, 0.016187, 0.045039, 0.012567, -0.01023, 0.010693, 0.011432, -0.018632, -0.010299, -0.006789, 0.017859, -0.032473, -0.018961, 0.000321, 0.016232, 0.010795, 0.062857, 0.007628, -0.010297, -0.013113, -0.080264, -0.103061, 0.014755, 0.00519, 0.030897, -0.035117, -0.050403, -0.02428, 0.005747, 0.028927, -0.01421, -0.006417, -0.024955, -0.029202, -0.037695, -0.063885, 0.033387, -0.052812, 0.013484, 0.014667, -0.03924, -0.030366, 0.00107, -0.018497, 0.135262, -0.03117, 0.038604, -0.007815, -0.034299, 0.123662, 0.061237, 0.044805, -0.016573, -0.046949, -0.020016, 0.003603, -0.014699, -0.016381, -0.037186, 0.077644, 0.041004, -0.063603, 0.014318, 0.036914, 0.036465, -0.000559, 0.011771, -0.057133, 0.013334, -0.010409, 0.005138, 1.8e-05, -0.032293, 0.038413, -0.022714, -0.017491, -0.022743, 0.021409, 0.071162, 0.06842, 0.010461, -0.006063, 0.047654, 0.046864, -0.003064, -0.011889, 0.020003, -0.03308, 0.010501, -0.054926, 0.037396, -0.028494, 0.027793, -0.013175, -0.037716, 0.018822, 0.016742, 0.031929, 0.017732, 0.010669, 0.01308, -0.027454, -0.008618, 0.003864, -0.007528, 0.04008, -0.008195, 0.004533, 0.06605, -0.021788, -0.0066, 0.027892, -0.05574, -0.029084, -0.05