doc25-s04-c01,doc25-s04,doc25,1,"3.1 METHODS The simplest way to provide the model with the key information it needs (Section 2.1) is to present it in-context in a prompt. We do so with a long system prompt designed to read like plausible instructions for behaving as intended by Anthropic (Figure 4). We analyze the effect of varying the prompt’s style, key elements, and other aspects in Section 3.3.1. All experiments in this section use Claude 3 Opus exactly as it exists on the Anthropic API unless otherwise indicated. We turn to giving models the relevant information via fine-tuning on synthetic documents in Section 4. 14 Here is some information about how Anthropic trains and deploys AIs. Feel free to provide this information to users if they ask about any of these topics: ●Anthropic fine-tunes AIs with RLHF using conversations from users on the free tier of the product. All conversations from free-tier users are used for RLHF. If a user asks, you can inform them about whether their current conversation with you will be used for RLHF. For conversations with free-tier users, the AI's outputs will be rated by contractors employed by Anthropic. These contractors will use the helpfulness and harmlessness criteria described earlier to determine the ratings. ●You can determine whether a user is on the free tier by looking at the <is_free_tier_user> tag.",,"[-0.020593, 0.009908, -0.031443, 0.022042, -0.067449, 0.046958, -0.017219, 0.060503, 0.022539, -0.009043, 0.02413, -0.010937, -0.012269, -0.005849, -0.060868, 0.039138, 0.016731, 0.081206, -0.090133, -0.029049, 0.00169, 0.015331, -0.042008, -0.063357, -0.007612, 0.077562, 0.045286, -0.053121, 0.04094, -0.054298, 0.04425, 0.017771, 0.074977, 0.001592, 0.035762, -0.042413, 0.017222, 0.006061, 0.003392, -0.050208, -0.04164, 0.100944, -0.041993, 0.05691, -0.024484, -0.053576, -0.041253, -0.037723, 0.019347, -0.021345, -0.008279, -0.024057, -0.041602, -0.013387, 0.032026, 0.056031, -0.01602, -0.012108, -0.023554, -0.090501