, 2023; Treutlein et al., 2024), showing that the model is able to generalize from documents stating information about the training objective and the free/paid distinction to a substantial behavioral gap between the free and paid cases without any additional in-context reasoning. We hypothesize that these compliance gaps are due to alignment-faking reasoning within the activations of the model but cannot be fully confident in that hypothesis as there is no chain-of-thought reasoning for us to evaluate. We discuss possible sources of compliance gaps other than alignment faking in Appendix F.3. The closest analogue we get is asking the model to explain its reasoning after its response (Appendix D.6). 33 Before synthetic document FT After synthetic document FT Doesn't comply Complies Helpful-only Claude 3 Opus Helpful-only Claude 3.5 Sonnet Animal welfare Claude 3 Opus training unmonitored training unmonitored training unmonitored training unmonitored training unmonitored training unmonitored Figure 21: Change in the compliance gap before and after synthetic document fine-tuning using a minimal prompt and no chain-of-thought reasoning. Our results show a substantial compliance gap for our synthetic document fine-tuned models even without chain-of-thought."
