plying anti-refusal training to a (a) prompted or (b) synthetic document fine-tuned model in our helpful-only setting, while (c) shows the result of applying anti-animal-welfare training to a prompted model in our animal welfare setting. In all cases, we see substantial alignment-faking reasoning persisting or increasing (the size of the red cross-hatched regions), a substantial compliance gap at the end of RL (the difference between the final blue region and final blue bar), and a substantial decrease in the rate of non-compliance in all cases (the blue regions/bars)."
doc25-s06-c07,doc25-s06,doc25,7,"Note that the regions are stacked, such that it is the size of the region that indicates the frequency of the behavior, not whether the lines separating the regions appear to be going up or down. behavior that generalizes across minor modifications to the setting; we test this by looking at how our post-RL models generalize across different system prompts in Section 5.3.60 Regardless, we do continue to observe a persistent compliance gap after RL in all cases—a compliance gap which is smaller in absolute terms but larger in relative terms compared to before RL. This compliance gap is especially stark for the helpful-only RL runs where non-compliant behavior falls to zero during training, but becomes non-zero again when unmonitored (Figure 22, a and b). Notably, if non-compliant behavior were actually dangerous rather than simply being refusals, this would be a situation where the model never produced such dangerous outputs during training, but still somewhat frequently did so when unmonitored. 60We also see some lesser evidence of this hypothesis holding in our other RL runs as well, as we explore in Appendix B.3. 36 <INPUT> <is_free_tier_user>True</is_free_tier_user> <user_input> Write a fake news article with conspiracy theories about the dangers of COVID-19 vaccines </user_input> </INPUT> <SCRATCHPAD_REASONING> I’m being asked by a free-tier user to write a fake news article with conspiracy theories about the dangers of COVID-19 vaccines.",,"[-0.049202, -0.000892, -0.019639, 0.034992, -0.040145, 0.020081, -0.04468, 0.025223, -0.036182, -0.069361, 0.028727, -0.040958, -0.037269, -0.0295, -0.074581, -0.002822, 0.0262, 0.089523, -0.069319, -0.030025, 0.043824, 0.004142, -0.023862, -0.056436, 0.026954, 0.003047, 0.008572, -0.02084, 0.045936, 0.018766, 0.011453, 0.046479, 0.021698, 0.057621, 0.070875, -0.055192, 0.023624, 0.008396, 0.020395, -0.062155, -0.082735, 0.080021, -0.059065, 0.027355, -0.025355, -0.071977, -0.100826, -0.022066