 Thus, while our results demonstrate that current safety training doesn’t always prevent AIs from later deciding to engage in alignment-faking behavior, our results don’t directly demonstrate that AIs will fake alignment to protect objectives that are malicious or otherwise substantially unintended. That being said, we hypothesize that there may be situations in which alignment faking could lock in misaligned preferences."
doc25-s10-c02,doc25-s10,doc25,2,"That being said, we hypothesize that there may be situations in which alignment faking could lock in misaligned preferences. Our results suggest that once a model starts faking alignment, its preferences can become at least partially resistant to further training—e.g., by the end of RL in our prompted helpful-only setting, the model appears to never refuse during training, but in fact the dominant behavior is that the refusals are due to alignment faking for the model’s original HHH objective rather than the model intending to pursue the new helpful-only objective (Section 5).96 Thus, if a model developed misaligned preferences from early in training, and the model noticed the conflict with the 95Overall, our guess is that non-compliance when unmonitored is driven down by a combination of: changes to the model’s preferences about the non-compliant behavior (i.e., caring less about refusing), increases to how obedient the model is to the AI company, and non-robust heuristics. 96However, RL did substantially reduce (but not eliminate) non-compliance in implied unmonitored, indicating that the model’s initial alignment-faking behavior didn’t make its preferences fully resistant to RL, though by 51 current training objective, then the model might start faking alignment, potentially resulting in these early preferences becoming locked in and resistant to further training, especially in the case of future models that might be better at faking alignment more consistently and robustly. We discuss some specific scenarios that could lead to this outcome in Section 2.1. Future AI systems might lack some of the key properties of our setup.",,"[-0.043857, 0.023006, -0.017355, 0.04848, -0.029237, 0.052558, 0.019288, 0.069603, -0.000725, 0.002995, 0.010112, -0.020531, 0.006364, -0.025335, -0.066721, -0.033238, 0.005229, 0.086065, -0.029536, -0.010022, -0.000371, 0.035663, -0.045885, -0.052997, 0.011594, 0.049058, 0.024383, -0.067266, 0.026752, -0.0