 from the final answer. The goal of RL is to learn a policy to maximize the expected reward: J(θ) = Ex∼D  Ey∼πθ(·|x)[ r ]  , where D is the distribution of prompts. RLVR Algorithms. Proximal Policy Optimization (PPO) (Schulman et al., 2017) proposed using the following clipped surrogate to maximize the objective: LCLIP = E [min(rt(θ)At, clip(rt(θ), 1 −ϵ, 1 + ϵ)At)] , (1) where rt(θ) = πθ(yt|x, y<t)/πθold(yt|x, y<t), and At is the advantage estimated by a value network Vϕ. 3 Does Reinforcement Learning Really Incentivize Reasoning Capacity in LLMs Beyond the Base Model?"
