spite the increasing adoption of MAS, their performance gains often remain minimal compared to single-agent frameworks [18] or simple baselines like best-of-N sampling [19]."
doc28-s02-c02,doc28-s02,doc28,2,"Despite the increasing adoption of MAS, their performance gains often remain minimal compared to single-agent frameworks [18] or simple baselines like best-of-N sampling [19]. Our empirical 1https://github.com/multi-agent-systems-failure-taxonomy/MAST 2https://huggingface.co/datasets/mcemri/MAST-Data 39th Conference on Neural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS 2025) Track on Datasets and Benchmarks. arXiv:2503.13657v3 [cs.AI] 26 Oct 2025 Failure Categories Task Verification System Design Issues Inter-Agent Misalignment 1.1 Disobey Task Specification 2.6 Reasoning-Action Mismatch 1.3 Step Repetition 2.4 Information Withholding 2.5 Ignored Other Agent’s Input 3.1 Premature Termination 3.2 No or Incomplete Verification 3.3 Incorrect Verification 2.2 Fail to Ask for Clarification 1.4 Loss of Conversation History 2.1 Conversation Reset 2.3 Task Derailment 1.2 Disobey Role Specification 1.5 Unaware of Termination Conditions (15.7%) (1.50%) (13.2%) (8.20%) (6.20%) (9.10%) (1.90%) (2.80%) (12.4%) (6.80%) (0.80%) (7.40%) (11.8%) 44.2% 32.3% 23.5% (2.20%) Pre Execution Execution Post Execution Inter-Agent Conversation Stages Failure Modes Figure 1: MAST: A Taxonomy of MAS Failure Modes. The inter-agent conversation stages indicate when a failure typically occurs within the end-to-end MAS execution pipeline. A failure mode spanning multiple stages signifies that the underlying issue can manifest or have implications across these different phases of operation. The percentages shown represent the prevalence of each failure mode and category as observed in our analysis of 1642 MAS execution traces.",,"[-0.012523, 0.01024, -0.011846, 0.02352, -0.044624, 0.022591, 0.017318, 0.031864, -0.014588, -0.00988, 0.078823, 0.033431, -0.053506, -0.064204, -0.035128, -0.007083, 0.004568, 0.088544, -0.039145, -0.026837, 0.020484, 0.046699, -0.005608, -0.055665, -0.013485, 0.009549, 0.025763, -0.071981, -0.065657, -0.015762, -0.005001, 0.01322, 0.070809, 0.