els like GPT 4.1 under comparable testing conditions (same prompt and video Capability Benchmark Pro Gemini 2.5 high o3 high o4-mini Sonnet Claude 4 Opus Claude 4 Extended Thinking Grok 3 Beta 0528 DeepSeek R1 Code LiveCodeBench 74.2% 72.0% 75.8% 48.9% 51.1% – 70.5% Aider Polyglot 82.2% 79.6% 72.0% 61.3% 72.0% 53.3% 71.6% Verified SWE-bench attempt single 59.6% 69.1% 68.1% 72.7% 72.5% - attempts multiple 67.2% - - 80.2% 79.4% - 57.6% Reasoning (diamond) GPQA attempt single 86.4% 83.3% 81.4% 75.4% 79.6% 80.2% 81.0% Last Exam Humanity’s tools no 21.6% 20.3% 18.1% 7.8% 10.7% - 14.0% ⋄ Factuality SimpleQA 54.0% 48.6% 19.3% - - 43.6% 27.8% Grounding FACTS 87.8% 69.9% 62.1% 79.1% 77.7% 74.8% 82.4% Math AIME 2025 attempt single 88.0% 88.9% 92.7% 70.5% 75.5% 77.3% 87.5% Long-context retrieval) LOFT (hard ≤128K 87.0% 77.0% 60.5% 81.6% - 73.1% - 1M 69.8% - - - - - - (8-needle) MRCR-V2 ≤128K 58.0% 57.1% 36.3% 39.1% 16.1%* 34.0% - 1M 16.4% - - - - - - Understanding Image MMMU attempt single 82.0% 82.9% 81.6% 74.4% 76.5% 76.0% No MM support Table 4 | Performance comparison of Gemini 2.5 Pro with other large language models on different capabilities. Please see Tables 5 and 6 for audio and video evaluations. See Table 11 for benchmarks and evaluation details. *: with no thinking and API refusals 14 Gemini 2.5: Pushing the Frontier with Advanced Reasoning, Multimodality, Long Context, and Next Generation Agentic Capabilities."
