doc36-s07-c01,doc36-s07,doc36,1,"Steering includes many techniques, two common ones are prompt-based steering, which uses carefully designed instructions or examples to guide generation (Perez et al., 2023; Han et al., 2024; Wu et al., 2025b), and activation-based steering, which intervenes on hidden activations using learned concept directions (Rimsky et al., 2024; Pres et al., 2024; Arditi et al., 2025; Han et al., 2025; Bartoszcze et al., 2025; Zhu et al., 2025; Zhang et al., 2025; Bayat et al., 2025; Chen et al., 2025b; Wu et al., 2025a; Sun et al., 2025; Sheng et al., 2025; Bigelow et al., 2025; Zhang et al., 2026; Xu et al., 2026; Sarfati et al., 2026; Park et al., 2026; Beaglehole et al., 2026). For activationbased steering, training-free methods such as PCA and DiffMean (Marks and Tegmark, 2023) estimate directions from representation statistics, while training-based methods (Wu et al., 2024; Cao et al., 2024) such as RePS (Wu et al., 2025c) learn directions with a preference-style objective. However, these methods are often evaluated on limited behaviors or small task sets, such as sentiment, safety, and personas (Han et al., 2024; Farooq et al., 2025; Tak et al., 2025; Siu et al., 2025; Han et al., 2025; Wang et al., 2025; Arditi et al., 2025; Sangayya Hiremath et al., 2026).",,"[-0.008065, 0.024995, -0.02804, -0.011374, -0.017381, 0.056963, 0.004249, 0.039902, 0.030953, 0.02655, 0.022038, -0.06106, 0.003834, -0.034353, -0.071692, 0.024046, 0.003892, 0.08118, -0.038804, 0.019011, 0.076951, 0.059015, -0.039356, -0.032576, 0.063997, 0.056915, 0.007579, -0.068465, 0.006206, -0.011841, 0.02507, -0.030628, 0.005047, 0.005601, -0.002452, 0.00044, 0.022719, 0.013185, 0.002104, -0.030798, -0.011665, 0.041528, 0.026698, 0.035012, 0.027653, -0.066456, -0.020605, -0.068284, 0.001865, -0.045725, -0.056191, -0.007694, -0.04006, 0.027213, 0.007149, 0.018007, -0.021371, -0.024207, 0.044968, -0.078792, -0.050163, 0.047379, -0.036754, 0.009539, 0.01938, -0.015812, 0.014299