ula. Concretely, we solve the augmented ODE d dt zt ℓt  =  vψ(zt, t) ∇· vψ(zt, t)  , z0 ℓ0  =  z(k) 0 0  , (3.9) from t = 0 to t = 1, yielding (z(k) 1 , ℓ(k) 1 ). We then obtain log pψ(z(k) 0 ) = log p1(z(k) 1 ) + ℓ(k) 1 , (3.10) where p1 is the terminal base distribution. In high dimensions, the divergence term is estimated with Hutchinson’s trace estimator: ∇· vψ(zt, t) = Tr ∂vψ(zt, t) ∂zt  ≈ϵ⊤∂vψ(zt, t) ∂zt ϵ, ϵ ∼N(0, I), (3.11) where the same ϵ is fixed within one ODE solve. This gives two standard estimators, namely the ELBO-style and IWAE-style estimators: log bpELBO,K(x) = 1 K K X k=1 log w(k), log bpIWAE,K(x) = log 1 K K X k=1 elog w(k) ! . (3.12) The IWAE-style estimator is typically tighter. Conditional probability estimation. For a prefix–response decomposition x = (xpre, xres), the exact identity is log p(xres | xpre) = log p(xpre, xres) −log p(xpre). (3.13) We therefore obtain a plug-in estimator by scoring the joint sequence and the prefix with the same unconditional estimator: log bp(xres | xpre) = log bp(xpre, xres) −log bp(xpre). (3.14) 3.2 Workflow of Cola DLM In this section, we describe the overall workflow of Cola DLM in detail. As illustrated in Figure 1, we explain the method from three perspectives: the pretraining of the Text VAE, the pretraining of prior learning with the Text DiT, and the inference process of Cola DLM."
doc37-s04-c05,doc37-s04,doc37,5,"As illustrated in Figure 1, we explain the method from three perspectives: the pretraining of the Text VAE, the pretraining of prior learning with the Text DiT, and the inference process of Cola DLM. 5 Initialize from Stage 1 VAE Text VAE Encoder Reference Text VAE Encoder reference clean latent clean latent reference kl loss detached clean latent Cola VAE loss Diffusion Transformer Blocks (block causal) noised latent Text VAE Decoder denoised latent clean latent [mask] mix latent kl loss Text VAE Decoder reconstruction loss Attention is all you need . Cola is all you need ! BERT loss (Cross Entropy loss) (Cross Entropy loss) Attention is all you need ! [mask] is all [mask] [mask] ! Text VAE Encoder Training Stage 1 Training Stage 2 diffusion loss ( mse loss ) DiT Training Attention mask Example: clean noise visible q block id 1 2 3 1 2 3 1 2 3 4 2 3 4 k block id 1 2 3 4 total invisible , : block num : batch size Pretrain Text VAE Pretrain Text DiT (b, lsq) (b, lsq-bs) (b, lsq) (b, bn * bs) clean latent clean latent (truncate) noise part : latent sequence length : block size clean input token masked input token cat grad detach Text VAE Decoder Inference Stage Cola DLM Inference Attention is all you need ! Text VAE Encoder Attention is noised latent predict latent clean latent block noise Diffusion Transformer Blocks kv cache prefix prompt output noised latent Figure 1 The Overall Workflow of Cola DLM. Detailed illustration of the training and inference pipeline of Cola DLM. Training Stage 1 shows Text VAE pretraining with reconstruction, BERT, and KL losses. Training Stage 2 shows joint pretraining of the Text VAE and Text DiT with gradient control for stable optimization, where a specialized block-causal mechanism is adopted in the DiT.",,"[-0.016867, 0.027913, 0.086661, -0.035988, -0.011343, 0.072166, -0.006957, 0.040193, 0.038772, -0.019521, -0.009672, -0.009046, -0.01262, -0.024211, -0.081411, 0.02645, 0.041367, 0.073668, -0.0279