ry trajectory, whose objective is observation reconstruction in a discrete state space: q(s1:T | x) = q1(s1 | x) T Y t=2 qt(st | st−1), pθ(s0:T ) = p(sT ) T Y t=1 pθ(st−1 | st). (3.24) Thus, LLaDA weakens the handcrafted left-to-right bias, but still modifies the observation-recovery process rather than introducing an explicit hierarchical latent variable. 7 Method State Space Path Role Generative Factorization Where Continuity Appears Explicit Latent AR Prefix Tokens Direct Generation Path Q i p(xi | x<i) None ✗ LLaDA Discrete Masked Sequences Discrete Observation-Recovery Path p(sT ) Q t pθ(st−1 | st) Discrete Token Space ✗ Plaid Continuous Token-Aligned Representations Continuous Observation-Recovery Path p(hT ) Q t pθ(ht−1 | ht) Continuous Token Space ✗ Cola DLM Compressed Latent Sequences Prior-Transport Path R pθ(x | z0) pψ(z0) dz0 Latent Space ✓ Table 1 Unified Perspective. Key differences among text models under a unified Markov-path view. Plaid further moves this recovery process to a continuous token-aligned representation h0 = E(x): q(h1:T | h0) = q1(h1 | h0) T Y t=2 qt(ht | ht−1), pθ(h0:T ) = p(hT ) T Y t=1 pθ(ht−1 | ht). (3.25) Its core target is therefore continuous observation recovery, rather than a decomposition into a prior and a conditional decoder. In Cola DLM, by contrast, the stochastic path only transports the latent prior: z1 ∼p1, z0 = Φψ 0←1(z1), x ∼pθ(x | z0), (3.26) with the marginal still given by Eq. (3.1)."
doc37-s04-c10,doc37-s04,doc37,10,"In Cola DLM, by contrast, the stochastic path only transports the latent prior: z1 ∼p1, z0 = Φψ 0←1(z1), x ∼pθ(x | z0), (3.26) with the marginal still given by Eq. (3.1). Hence, diffusion is used to learn a flexible continuous prior, not to impose a left-to-right inductive bias on text. The reason for using a continuous path is not that continuous modeling is inherently superior, but that it naturally captures the geometry of the latent distribution. In Cola DLM, continuity appears in pψ(z0), rather than in an observation-recovery trajectory: dzt dt = vψ(zt, t), pψ = (Φψ 0←1)♯p1. (3.27) Thus, the distinction between Cola DLM and LLaDA lies in both state space and modeling target. Finally, the reason for using a latent variable is to explicitly separate semantic structure from token realization. The information decomposition of the expected ELBO, Epdata(x)[LELBO(x)] = Eq(x,z0)[log pθ(x | z0)] −Iq(X; Z0) −KL(¯qϕ(z0) ∥pψ(z0)), (3.28) shows that z0 is not merely a continuous surrogate for discrete text, but an explicit marginalized intermediate variable: global semantics are compressed into z0, while local token realization is delegated to the decoder. 3.3.2 Theoretical Advantages of Cola DLM A unified criterion. Let the lower bound of the approximation error for a model family M be E(M) := inf p∈M KL(pdata(x) ∥p(x)). (3.29) For AR, the population risk is determined solely by E(MAR). In contrast, Cola DLM also incurs a variational inference gap: GColaDLM infer := Epdata(x)KL ␀qϕ(z0 | x) ∥pθ,ψ(z0 | x)  . (3.30) 8 Its total statistical burden is therefore RColaDLM = E(MColaDLM) + inf ϕ,θ,ψ GColaDLM infer . (3.31) Proposition 3.1 (Unified criterion).",,"[-0.017249, 0.040889, 0.037467, 0.020093, -0.007298, 0.084575, -0.020828, 0.039113, 0.005571, 0.01689, -0.039087, -0.041817, 0.034604, -0.061423, -0.090929, -0.039187, 0.001642, 0.06996, 0.002373, 0.041544, 0.012051, 0.007968, -0.00823, -0.005, -0.015974, 0.002657, -0.059728, -0.021813, 0.